X('volumetric-weight-air-freight',[
 ('Three more worked examples',[('table',['Box (cm)','Actual kg','Volumetric kg','Charged'],[['50 x 40 x 30','12','10','12'],['100 x 60 x 60','25','60','60'],['120 x 80 x 100 pallet','200','160','200']],'Volumetric weight = length x width x height in cm, divided by 6,000.')]),
 ('Several pieces in one shipment',['The airline adds up the actual weight and the volumetric weight of all pieces, then charges the larger total. Mixing a few dense pieces with a few bulky ones averages out, so it helps to ship them together rather than separately.']),
 ('Reduce it',['Use the smallest carton that protects the goods, remove void space, and consider shipping bulky items knocked down and assembled at destination. Check the result with the <a href="container-load-planner" style="color:#0A6CC2">load planner</a> if you are shipping by sea instead.'])],
 [('Is volumetric weight used in sea freight?','Not in the same way. In FCL you pay for the container. In LCL you pay by the greater of cubic metres or tonnes, so the idea is similar but the unit is different.')])
X('fcl-vs-lcl-shipping',[
 ('A simple way to compare',['Ask for an FCL quote and an LCL quote on the same lane and compare the cost per cubic metre actually used. If the LCL cost for your volume is near the FCL price, take the FCL. You also avoid the extra handling that LCL needs, and your cargo does not wait for the consolidator to fill the box.']),
 ('Things people forget about LCL',['LCL cargo is stuffed at a CFS and unstuffed at a CFS at the other end, and each step carries a charge and a delay.','Several shippers share one container, so a problem with another shipper’s cargo can hold up yours.','The destination customs clearance is done per consignment, so you still need your own documents.']),
 ('When FCL is worth it even for part loads',['Fragile or high value cargo, cargo with strict delivery dates, and goods that must not be mixed with others, such as food next to chemicals. See the <a href="guides/how-lcl-consolidation-works" style="color:#0A6CC2">LCL consolidation guide</a> and the <a href="container-load-planner" style="color:#0A6CC2">free load planner</a> to see what fits.'])],
 [('Can I ship part of a container myself and share the rest?','Some forwarders offer shared container or buyer consolidation, where several of your suppliers load into one box. Ask your forwarder.')])
X('ocean-freight-surcharges-explained',[
 ('How to read a sea freight quote',['Start with the base ocean freight, then add everything that is quoted separately. Typical lines are the bunker or fuel adjustment, the currency adjustment, the terminal handling charge at each end, the documentation fee, the container seal and the peak season surcharge when it applies. Ask for every line to be shown and for the currency of each.']),
 ('Charges that arrive later',['Detention and demurrage if containers are not returned or collected in time, see <a href="guides/demurrage-and-detention-explained" style="color:#0A6CC2">demurrage and detention</a>.','Examination, weighment and special handling charges at the port or depot.','Amendment fees if the bill of lading has to be changed.']),
 ('How to avoid surprises',['Compare quotes on the same basis, for example CIF to the destination or FOB at the origin. Ask what happens to the quote if the sailing is delayed or the booking is rolled. A fair forwarder will explain each charge.'])],
 [('Who pays the origin and destination charges?','It depends on the Incoterm and the terms agreed in the contract. Under FOB the buyer usually pays the ocean freight and the destination charges. Under CIF the seller pays the freight but not the destination handling.')])
X('delhi-ncr-icds-tughlakabad-dadri-patparganj',[
 ('Choosing between the depots',['The right depot depends on where your factory or warehouse is, which port the cargo comes through and which rail services run on that corridor. Dadri is close to Noida and Ghaziabad. Tughlakabad sits in south Delhi, and Patparganj in east Delhi. Compare the truck distance, the rail schedule and the depot charges for your actual case, not the general reputation of each depot.']),
 ('How the rail leg works',['A container that is cleared inland first moves from the port to the depot under customs control on a bond. The shipping line or rail operator issues the movement documents, and the container is declared at the depot. Clearance happens there and the container is released for delivery. The cost and the time are different from clearing at the port, so ask your forwarder to quote both. See <a href="guides/icd-vs-cfs-vs-port-explained" style="color:#0A6CC2">ICD vs CFS vs port</a>.']),
 ('Our pages for each depot',['<a href="icd-tughlakabad-customs-clearance" style="color:#0A6CC2">ICD Tughlakabad</a> and <a href="icd-dadri-customs-clearance" style="color:#0A6CC2">ICD Dadri</a>, and the overview of <a href="customs-clearance-delhi" style="color:#0A6CC2">customs clearance in Delhi</a>.'])],
 [('Does inland clearance cost more?','It adds the rail or road leg and depot charges, but it can save port detention and congestion, and the cargo clears close to your factory. Compare the total, not the single line.')])
X('mundra-port-guide',[
 ('Who uses Mundra',['Importers and exporters in Gujarat, Rajasthan, Punjab, Haryana and Delhi NCR commonly use Mundra, because of its rail links and the number of services calling there. Containers, bulk cargo, vehicles and liquids are all handled at different terminals in the port area.']),
 ('Getting cargo in and out',['By road, from the factory to the port gate against a gate pass. By rail, from the port rail yard to inland depots such as Tughlakabad and Dadri. For exports, the container is gated in before the cut-off for the vessel, with the shipping bill and the other documents in order.']),
 ('Local knowledge matters',['Terminal rules, truck booking and gate timings change, and having an office on site helps. Our team works from the Adani Ports and SEZ and can tell you what is happening this week. See our <a href="mundra-port-customs-clearance" style="color:#0A6CC2">Mundra clearance page</a> or compare with <a href="guides/jnpt-nhava-sheva-port-guide" style="color:#0A6CC2">Nhava Sheva</a>.'])],
 [('Is Mundra a government port?','No. Mundra is a private port operated by Adani Ports and Special Economic Zone, in Kachchh, Gujarat.')])
X('jnpt-nhava-sheva-port-guide',[
 ('Who uses Nhava Sheva',['Importers and exporters across Maharashtra, Karnataka, Madhya Pradesh and beyond use JNPT, and it is also a main gateway to north India by rail. Several container terminals operate within the port, and the terminal your cargo uses depends on the shipping line.']),
 ('Direct port delivery',['Under direct port delivery the container goes from the port to the importer’s premises without a stop at a CFS, which can save time and charges. It is open to approved importers and depends on the terminal and the shipping line, so ask your broker if you qualify.']),
 ('What to watch',['Truck congestion at the gate in peak periods, the free time on the container, and the cut-off for export containers. Our <a href="nhava-sheva-jnpt-customs-clearance" style="color:#0A6CC2">Nhava Sheva clearance page</a> explains what we do there, and the <a href="guides/mundra-vs-jnpt-which-port" style="color:#0A6CC2">Mundra vs JNPT</a> guide helps you choose.'])],
 [('What does JNPT stand for?','Jawaharlal Nehru Port Trust, now Jawaharlal Nehru Port Authority. The port is at Nhava Sheva near Navi Mumbai and is also called Nhava Sheva.')])
X('mundra-vs-jnpt-which-port',[
 ('Questions to ask for your own cargo',['Where is the factory or warehouse? The closer port is not always cheaper if the rail link from the other is faster.','Which shipping lines and services do you need, and do they call at both?','What is the free time, the terminal charge and the cost of the inland leg at each?','Do you want to clear at the port or at an inland depot such as Dadri?']),
 ('Example',['An importer in Ludhiana with cargo from the Far East compares the two. The rail from Mundra to the northern depot takes fewer days, so Mundra may suit. An importer in Pune with the same cargo will usually find JNPT closer and cheaper. The point is to compare the total landed cost for your own lane, not to pick a favourite port.']),
 ('Our pages',['Read about <a href="mundra-port-customs-clearance" style="color:#0A6CC2">Mundra</a> and <a href="nhava-sheva-jnpt-customs-clearance" style="color:#0A6CC2">Nhava Sheva</a> and ask us for a side-by-side quote.'])],
 [('Can I switch ports after booking?','Sometimes, if the line allows a port change before the vessel sails, but it can mean extra charges. Decide before you book.')])
X('icd-vs-cfs-vs-port-explained',[
 ('Cost and time compared',[('table',['','Port','CFS','ICD'],[['Where','At the seaport','Near the port','Inland, rail linked'],['Used for','Direct delivery, FCL','LCL and some FCL','Clearance near the factory'],['Main saving','Speed','Handling of small cargo','Less port congestion and detention']],'Costs vary by location and cargo. Ask for each option quoted.')]),
 ('How to pick',['If the cargo is LCL, a CFS is usual. If the factory is far inland and the box is FCL, an ICD can save money and time. If you need the cargo fast and the port is close, clearing at the port is simplest. Your broker can quote all three for the same shipment.'])],
 [('Does the choice change the duty?','No. The duty depends on the goods and their value, not on where the bill of entry is cleared. Charges for handling and transport differ.')])
X('how-to-export-from-india-step-by-step',[
 ('Costs and money to plan for',['Cost of production and packing, inland transport, port or airport handling, ocean or air freight, insurance and the broker and forwarder fees. Add the cost of finance while you wait for payment, and the bank charges for the remittance. See <a href="guides/trade-finance-options-for-exporters" style="color:#0A6CC2">trade finance options</a> and <a href="guides/ecgc-export-credit-insurance" style="color:#0A6CC2">ECGC cover</a> if the buyer is new.']),
 ('Schemes that can improve your margin',['Drawback and RoDTEP refund duties and taxes embedded in the export. GST on exports is zero rated, either under a letter of undertaking or by paying IGST and claiming a refund. See the guides on <a href="guides/duty-drawback-explained" style="color:#0A6CC2">drawback</a>, <a href="guides/rodtep-explained" style="color:#0A6CC2">RoDTEP</a> and <a href="guides/gst-lut-export-letter-of-undertaking" style="color:#0A6CC2">LUT</a>.']),
 ('After the shipment leaves',['Send the buyer the documents, collect payment through the bank, and keep the proof of realisation. Many export benefits depend on it, see <a href="guides/export-proceeds-realisation-fema-ebrc" style="color:#0A6CC2">export proceeds realisation</a>.'])],
 [('Do I need an IEC to export?','Yes, in nearly all cases. Get it before you file the first shipping bill.')])
X('shipping-bill-explained',[
 ('Types of shipping bill',['A free shipping bill is for goods exported without duty or benefit. A drawback shipping bill is for exports that claim drawback. A dutiable shipping bill is for goods that carry export duty. Others cover exports from bond, from an SEZ or under particular schemes. Your broker picks the right one for the cargo.']),
 ('What happens after filing',['The system may pass the bill straight through or ask for an examination. When the officer is satisfied, the let export order is given, and the container is stuffed and sealed or loaded at the port. The airline or shipping line then carries the goods.']),
 ('Mistakes to avoid',['A wrong invoice value, a wrong HS code or a wrong export scheme code can cost you the benefit. Check the draft before it is submitted, and keep copies of the invoice, packing list and bill of lading for your records. See also the <a href="guides/export-documents-checklist" style="color:#0A6CC2">export documents checklist</a>.'])],
 [('Can a shipping bill be amended?','In many cases yes, before or after the let export order, but amendments need reasons and approvals, and some cost a fee. It is easier to get it right the first time.')])
